@@ -13,6 +13,9 @@ of its booking desk, written in TypeScript with no runtime dependency.
 - `book({ itemId, start, end })`: returns `{ id, itemId, start, end, total }`; booking ids are sequential (`booking-1`, ...) so that runs are deterministic.
 - `availability({ start, end, kind? })`: returns the sorted ids of the equipment of that `kind` (any kind when omitted) with no booking overlapping the period, so the desk sees what can still be rented. It throws for a period that is not whole days or an unknown `kind`.
 
+A rental of 3 days or more costs 10% less than its full price (rounded half up to the cent); `quote` and `book`
+both return the reduced `total`.
+
 Both `quote` and `book` throw for an unknown item or a period that is not whole days (`start` and `end` are ISO-8601 UTC strings at
 midnight, `end` being the start of the day after the last day, so it must be after `start`). `book` also throws if the
 item already has an overlapping booking; a booking ending the day another starts is fine.
